  "text": "Join a hackathon \nHost a hackathon \nResources \nLog in\nSign up\nTerms Desk\n\nDecides, per PayPal invoice, whether an early-payment discount earns cash or just gives margin away. Nothing is sent without human approval.\n\n Like  Comment\nSTORY\nUPDATES\nSUBMISSION HISTORY\n\n1\n2\n\nPre-existing work disclosure: Terms Desk was built in October 2026 for the PayPal AI Hackathon on Devpost and is submitted here as a pre-existing project. The code, model, backtest and sandbox flow predate this event.\n\nInspiration\n\n\"2/10 net 30\" looks small, but it costs a merchant about 37% a year. Many freelancers and small businesses offer early-payment discounts to everyone, including clients who would pay on time anyway.\n\nWhat it does\nPredict: per-client probability of paying on time, from payment history a merchant already has.\nSkeptic (deterministic, not AI): expected-value check that blocks any discount that loses money.\nApproval queue: nothing is sent until a human clicks approve.\nAct: creates and sends the PayPal invoice with the discount, then resets it to full price if still unpaid when the window closes.\nLedger: logs every blocked discount and the money it saved.\nHow we built it\n\nXGBoost on a public CC0 \"Payment Date Dataset\" (41,555 closed B2B invoices; train 2019, test 2020; history features use only invoices cleared before each posting date, so no leakage). PayPal Invoicing v2 API in the sandbox. Static web walkthrough.\n\nResults\n\nROC AUC 0.783 on the 2020 test set vs 0.749 for a client-history baseline. One verified end-to-end PayPal sandbox run: a $2,000 invoice with a 2% discount was paid at $1,960. Sandbox only, no real money.\n\nWhat's next\n\nRe-run the backtest on the original Kaggle file, test on freelancer-style invoice data, and add a daily scheduler for enforcement.\n\nBuilt With\ncss\nhtml\njavascript\npaypal-invoicing-api\npython\nscikit-learn\nxgboost\nTry it out\n GitHub Repo\n aryanrsinghsengar.github.io\nSUBMITTED TO\n\nLaunchPad Hacks\n\nSLAY HACKS\n\nCREATED BY\nAaryan singh \n\n\n Like \nUpdates\n\nAaryan singh started this project — 7 days ago\n\nLeave feedback in the comments!\n\nLog in or sign up for Devpost to join the conversation.\n\nSubmission history\nDevpost\nAbout\nCareers\nContact\nHelp\nHackathons\nBrowse hackathons\nExplore projects\nHost a hackathon\nHackathon guides\nPortfolio\nYour projects\nYour hackathons\nSettings\nConnect\n Twitter\n Discord\n Facebook\n LinkedIn\n© 2026 Devpost, Inc. All rights reserved.\nCommunity guidelines\nSecurity\nCA notice\nPrivacy policy\nTerms of service",
